1
00:05:31,764 --> 00:05:37,764
Fear in the Night is a mystery, thriller, horror
film directed by Jimmy Sangster.

2
00:11:03,529 --> 00:11:09,529
It took Peggy Heller a long time to recover from the trauma of a
brutal physical assault, suffered in her youth.

3
00:16:35,294 --> 00:16:41,294
When she married Robert, he provided her with the love and reassurance she craved for and the two
settled down in a pretty house in the grounds of the public school where Robert was a master.

4
00:22:07,058 --> 00:22:13,058
But the headmaster of the school is not what he seems and Peggy is convinced he means to harm her - is her fear a figment of her
tortured imagination or are there forces at work that intend to manipulate her anxieties with fatal consequences?

5
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:44,823
Molly Carmichael, played by Joan Collins.

6
00:33:10,588 --> 00:33:16,588
Michael Carmichael, played by Peter Cushing.

7
00:38:42,352 --> 00:38:48,352
Peggy Heller, played by Judy Geeson.

8
00:44:14,117 --> 00:44:20,117
Robert Heller, played by Ralph Bates.

9
00:49:45,882 --> 00:49:51,882
The Doctor, played by James Cossins.

10
00:55:17,647 --> 00:55:23,647
Mrs. Beamish, played by Gillian Lind.

11
01:00:49,411 --> 01:00:55,411
Fear in the Night (also known as Dynasty of Fear and Honeymoon of Fear) is a 1972 British psychological horror film directed, produced, and
co-written by Jimmy Sangster, produced by Hammer Film Productions, and starring Judy Geeson, Joan Collins, Peter Cushing, and Ralph Bates.

12
01:06:21,176 --> 01:06:27,176
It focuses on a psychologically fragile woman who, upon relocating to a rural boarding school where her husband
has taken a job, finds herself being tormented by a mysterious figure with a prosthetic arm.

13
01:11:52,941 --> 01:11:58,941
Like many horror films of its era, Fear in the Night has been noted for its usage of female hysteria as a central narrative motif, and was
released as a double bill in the United Kingdom with Straight on Till Morning, another Hammer film featuring similar themes.

14
01:17:24,705 --> 01:17:30,705
In the United States, the film was released as part of
a double bill with Demons of the Mind.

15
01:22:56,470 --> 01:23:02,470
The film explores themes of murder, psychological thriller,
nervous breakdown, newlywed, schoolhouse.

16
01:28:28,235 --> 01:28:34,235
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
